   - C1 known-good: declared F1 pin equals live F1 sha.
   - C2 mutation: in-memory copy of F1 bytes with one byte flipped must yield MISMATCH (same instrument function, temp file under artifacts/worker-070/.../control/, then deleted; do NOT touch canonical).
   - C3 missing: a synthetic nonexistent path must yield MISSING.
   - C4 hash-index: a temp file with a known sha must be found by the index.
   - C5 self-reference: verify FROZEN.json does NOT pin itself (self_reference note) — i.e., no pin path resolves to FROZEN.json.
